ob("migrate.v1", "Version 1 (the old sick-day log) becomes version 2 by building a fresh empty log that takes over only children, episodes, measurements, meds (or the two starting medicines) and settings (over the defaults); each entry gets the child of its illness; the selected child is the first child that is not deleted. Nothing else is carried over.", ex("migrate", 1, 2) + t("migrate", "old_entries_get_their_child_from_the_illness"))
ob("migrate.v2", "Version 2 becomes 3 by moving the book photos kept in vaccines and checkups (kind 'page') into documents and pages, with deterministic ids, times and tombstones, so two phones that upgrade separately end up with the same log.", ex("migrate", 3, 4, 5) + t("migrate", "every_photo_becomes_one_page_and_a_tombstone", "upgrading_twice_gives_the_same_log"))
ob("migrate.keep-before", "Adding a collection or fields needs no version change (older apps keep parts they do not know); changing what existing data means needs the next version, a migration step and a test. Before a migration step runs, the log as it was is kept: as 'before-vN' (N the new version) in the phone's database and as backups/aura-log-before-vN.json in Drive (once); these copies are never pruned. An older app never writes a newer log.", kind="constraint", reason="A bad migration must always be undoable by the parent.", unchecked="An end-to-end test that upgrades a saved old log on the phone and in a Drive stand-in and finds both copies, then runs the previous version's build against the new log and sees nothing written.")
ob("migrate.v-less-log", "A log without a valid v is treated as version 1. The step from 1 to 2 converts the old collections and keeps every other collection and field of the log as it is, so a damaged or hand-edited log never loses data.", ex("migrate", 7, 8, 11), kind="behaviour")
